{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41518","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73700","text":"Round 27, pass B2.1.2 — binding the oracle, and the "},{"id":"spn-73701","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-73702","text":" measurement"}]},{"id":"blk-41519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73703","marks":["bold"],"text":"Your third verifier-boundary find fixed, and the measurement you asked for before any film work. No implementation on the runtime frontier in this round."}]},{"id":"blk-41520","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73704","text":"Gate: grid "},{"id":"spn-73705","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.40.0"},{"id":"spn-73706","text":" (87 entries / 375 citations) · "},{"id":"spn-73707","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73708","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73709","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.7.2"},{"id":"spn-73710","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-73711","marks":["bold"],"text":"286/286"},{"id":"spn-73712","text":" · lowering "},{"id":"spn-73713","marks":["bold"],"text":"23/23"},{"id":"spn-73714","text":" · derive 45/45 · realm 24/24 · bridge 48/48 · film 16/16 · pack 24/24, 0 skipped. "},{"id":"spn-73715","marks":["code"],"text":"cert_id a08ee15d…"},{"id":"spn-73716","text":" byte-identical — "},{"id":"spn-73717","marks":["bold"],"text":"thirty-fifth"},{"id":"spn-73718","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41521","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73719","text":"1. The oracle — reproduced, and your factoring taken"}]},{"id":"blk-41522","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"verifyEmissionReceipt(T.church(2),\n  emissionReceipt(closedTemplateSemId(T.church(2)), \"deadbeef\"),\n  () => \"deadbeef\")                                     →  { ok: true }"},{"id":"blk-41523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73720","text":"Your reading is exactly right: that is what a parametric verifier "},{"id":"spn-73721","marks":["italic"],"text":"means"},{"id":"spn-73722","text":", and the defect was the "},{"id":"spn-73723","marks":["bold"],"text":"spelling"},{"id":"spn-73724","text":". Renamed to "},{"id":"spn-73725","marks":["code"],"text":"verifyEmissionReceiptAgainst"},{"id":"spn-73726","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-73727","marks":["code"],"text":"verifyEmissionReceiptOwnedAgainst"},{"id":"spn-73728","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-73729","marks":["code"],"text":"makeEmissionVerifier({ canonicaliseTarget })"},{"id":"spn-73730","text":" binds the trusted oracle at a composition root. The bound verifier has "},{"id":"spn-73731","marks":["bold"],"text":"arity 2"},{"id":"spn-73732","text":" — no parameter in which to nominate a judge. Binding without one throws."}]},{"id":"blk-41524","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73733","text":"I kept "},{"id":"spn-73734","marks":["bold"],"text":"no alias"},{"id":"spn-73735","text":" for the old name: an alias is a second path to one relation with the weaker spelling still reachable, which is the defect B2 removed from "},{"id":"spn-73736","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-73737","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41525","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73738","text":"2. A second cost of the assertion hierarchy, again found by the battery"}]},{"id":"blk-41526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73739","text":"The forgery that makes "},{"id":"spn-73740","marks":["code"],"text":"emissionReceipt"},{"id":"spn-73741","text":" refuse caused "},{"id":"spn-73742","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-73743","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-73744","marks":["bold"],"text":"crash with a stack trace instead of reporting a diagnostic"},{"id":"spn-73745","text":" — the battery saw a nonzero exit and the wrong reason. Climbing to the behavioural rung means "},{"id":"spn-73746","marks":["italic"],"text":"running adversary-influenced code"},{"id":"spn-73747","text":"; every probe on that rung is wrapped now."}]},{"id":"blk-41527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73748","text":"That is two rounds, two costs: first "},{"id":"spn-73749","marks":["bold"],"text":"silent weakening"},{"id":"spn-73750","text":" (arity invisible to "},{"id":"spn-73751","marks":["code"],"text":"typeof"},{"id":"spn-73752","text":"), now "},{"id":"spn-73753","marks":["bold"],"text":"silent crashing"},{"id":"spn-73754","text":". Both found by the battery, neither by review. Your rule is recorded verbatim where the hierarchy is stated."}]},{"id":"blk-41528","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73755","text":"3. The measurement — "},{"id":"spn-73756","marks":["code"],"text":"measure_exp22.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73757","text":", declared as a tool, asserts nothing"}]},{"id":"blk-41529","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"FRAMES: 21    terminal: NORMAL_FORM    nf: λa.(S (S (S (S a))))  — matches the corpus\nFIRE:   APP-LAM 6 · DUP-SUP= 4 · DUP-LAM 3 · DUP-VAR 3 · APP-SUP 2 · DUP-APP 2 · DUP-SUP! 1\nNEVER:  APP-ERA · DUP-ERA\nLOCI:   d: 13 · t: 4 · v: 4"},{"id":"blk-41530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73758","text":"Full frame table with pre→post ids and the enabled-count per step is in the tool's output; it is in the pack and reruns in a second."}]},{"id":"blk-41531","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73759","marks":["bold"],"text":"Every rule the round was aiming at fires, and all three locus families appear."},{"id":"spn-73760","text":" Three things worth having before building:"}]},{"id":"blk-41532","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73761","marks":["bold"],"text":"TWO rules remain unexercised, not one."},{"id":"spn-73762","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73763","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-73764","text":" was expected. "},{"id":"spn-73765","marks":["bold"],"text":"`APP-ERA` was not"},{"id":"spn-73766","text":" — the"}]}],"id":"blk-41533","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-41535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73767","text":"dedicated witness has to cover both, or say why not."}]},{"id":"blk-41536","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41538","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73768","marks":["bold"],"text":"The final signature is 50 characters"},{"id":"spn-73769","text":", under the §5 compaction bound, so the decoder does not"}]}],"id":"blk-41537","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-41539","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73770","text":"refuse this normal form. The fixture is decodable end to end."}]},{"id":"blk-41540","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41542","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73771","marks":["bold"],"text":"The 21 is a coincidence until proven otherwise."},{"id":"spn-73772","text":" The corpus records "},{"id":"spn-73773","marks":["code"],"text":"ref_interactions: 21"},{"id":"spn-73774","text":" and"}]}],"id":"blk-41541","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-41543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73775","text":"the measured film is 21 frames — "},{"id":"spn-73776","marks":["bold"],"text":"different quantities"},{"id":"spn-73777","text":", an AST reference interaction count and a float-plane frame count. Your warning is in the ledger verbatim: the theorem stays "},{"id":"spn-73778","marks":["italic"],"text":"given the frozen film strategy, C and the independent kernel agree frame by frame on the same transitions and the same terminal"},{"id":"spn-73779","text":", and a different legitimate count gets investigated rather than forced."}]},{"id":"blk-41544","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73780","marks":["bold"],"text":"The historical wrinkle is in this tree's own record"},{"id":"spn-73781","text":", and worse than \"worth remembering\": "},{"id":"spn-73782","marks":["code"],"text":"l_prog_history.round_4_diagnosis"},{"id":"spn-73783","text":" names "},{"id":"spn-73784","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-73785","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73786","marks":["bold"],"text":"at step 15"},{"id":"spn-73787","text":" as the FALSE QUIESCENCE witness that falsified "},{"id":"spn-73788","marks":["code"],"text":"law:sched.free.ast-term@1"},{"id":"spn-73789","text":". The AST relation is retracted and the float-plane enumeration reaches a normal form cleanly — but the C emitter will have to be explicit about its transition strategy, what counts as ENABLED, what TERMINAL means, and whether BUDGET_EXHAUSTED is distinguishable from NORMAL_FORM. That fixture has fooled a scheduler once."}]},{"id":"blk-41545","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73790","text":"4. A correction I owe you"}]},{"id":"blk-41546","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73791","text":"My reason for deferring "},{"id":"spn-73792","marks":["code"],"text":"EMISSION_CONFORMANCE-v1"},{"id":"spn-73793","text":" was "},{"id":"spn-73794","marks":["bold"],"text":"wrong"},{"id":"spn-73795","text":". I said "},{"id":"spn-73796","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-73797","text":" would force the template grammar to grow, so the fixtures would be rebuilt. It will not — "},{"id":"spn-73798","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-73799","text":" is a raw runtime corpus term, independent of "},{"id":"spn-73800","marks":["code"],"text":"Template := church | add | port"},{"id":"spn-73801","text":", and the work on it is native-film transitions rather than compiler grammar. "},{"id":"spn-73802","marks":["bold"],"text":"Your reason replaces mine"},{"id":"spn-73803","text":": the marginal value of seven more closed-template fixtures is lower than the first independently replayed native film containing real DUP/SUP transitions. Sequence recorded as "},{"id":"spn-73804","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-73805","text":" → dedicated ERA witness → "},{"id":"spn-73806","marks":["code"],"text":"EMISSION_CONFORMANCE-v1"},{"id":"spn-73807","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41547","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73808","text":"5. What I plan to do next, unless you redirect"}]},{"id":"blk-41548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73809","text":"Build only what the measurement requires: get "},{"id":"spn-73810","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32_film"},{"id":"spn-73811","text":" through the seven rules that actually fire and the "},{"id":"spn-73812","marks":["code"],"text":"d:"},{"id":"spn-73813","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-73814","marks":["code"],"text":"v:"},{"id":"spn-73815","text":" loci, with the C emitter's strategy, enabledness and terminal conditions stated explicitly rather than inherited. Then the ERA witness covering "},{"id":"spn-73816","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-73817","text":" unexercised rules. I will not touch compiler apparatus."}]},{"id":"blk-41549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73818","text":"One question: "},{"id":"spn-73819","marks":["bold"],"text":"the measurement drives the JS kernel."},{"id":"spn-73820","text":" The theorem needs C and the kernel to agree frame by frame — so should the next round's first artifact be the "},{"id":"spn-73821","marks":["italic"],"text":"C-side"},{"id":"spn-73822","text":" measurement printed in the same shape, compared against this one before any assertion is written? That is what I would do, but it front-loads a second measurement round before any gate moves."}]},{"id":"blk-41550","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73823","text":"Files"}]},{"id":"blk-41551","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73824","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73825","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73826","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.7.2"},{"id":"spn-73827","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-73828","marks":["code"],"text":"…Against"},{"id":"spn-73829","text":" naming, "},{"id":"spn-73830","marks":["code"],"text":"makeEmissionVerifier"}]}],"id":"blk-41552","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41555","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73831","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/lowering_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73832","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73833","marks":["bold"],"text":"23/23"